peed therefore have a\ndisproportionate effect on the power.","position":{"start":{"line":178,"column":1},"end":{"line":178,"column":1}},"key":"ljzyznHMX1"}],"key":"ZNHsAh00Oz"}],"key":"G4krQLJle6"},{"type":"listItem","spread":true,"position":{"start":{"line":183,"column":1},"end":{"line":186,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A strongly fluctuating electrical power stresses the power grid and the\npower electronics of the turbine. In practice, the turbine must cushion\nthe fluctuations, for example by controlling the rotor blades, by buffer\nstorage or by feeding into the grid only above a minimum wind speed.","position":{"start":{"line":183,"column":1},"end":{"line":183,"column":1}},"key":"Q3jUBg8llY"}],"key":"lqlSqNIkww"}],"key":"sKk7wTrezU"}],"key":"cVJoAvm8dm"}],"class":"tip dropdown","key":"Jq5QI2j7d3"},{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Bonus exercise: Second site (✩✩✩)","position":{"start":{"line":189,"column":1},"end":{"line":189,"column":1}},"key":"lHYcZZdQEm"}],"key":"vilz6fcpuy"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":191,"column":1},"end":{"line":192,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"A second test run at a windier site delivers the following wind speeds (m/s)\nat the same eight points in time:","position":{"start":{"line":191,"column":1},"end":{"line":191,"column":1}},"key":"H91Q6Ghx6P"}],"key":"PQDLJUjzqk"},{"type":"code","lang":"text","value":"7.5, 8.1, 6.9, 9.2, 8.8, 7.6, 8.4, 9.0","position":{"start":{"line":194,"column":1},"end":{"line":196,"column":1}},"key":"RHL9dyG0wI"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":198,"column":1},"end":{"line":201,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Carry out the calculation from Part 1 to Part 5 for this second site. The\ntime axis and the efficiency curve depend only on the start-up time, not on\nthe site, and therefore remain unchanged. Which site delivers more power on\naverage? Which delivers the more even power relative to the mean?","position":{"start":{"line":198,"column":1},"end":{"line":198,"column":1}},"key":"oquJn3rQCk"}],"key":"QFCRxkJt4w"}],"class":"tip","key":"W0vf1WFkU8"}],"key":"iTta0mHGzH"},{"type":"block","kind":"notebook-code","children":[{"type":"code","lang":"python","executable":true,"value":"# code cell","key":"pGKi8yemcm"},{"type":"outputs","id":"0NfjrIz-_5lYgsWHcFIZx","children":[],"key":"QDUgzjqdFu"}],"key":"WaIQG0vrJO"},{"type":"block","children":[{"type":"admonition","children":[{"type":"admonitionTitle","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Solution bonus exercise","position":{"start":{"line":208,"column":1},"end":{"line":208,"column":1}},"key":"FvD5oaDIZR"}],"key":"W70CyN0D5J"},{"type":"code","lang":"python","value":"wind_speed_2 = np.array([7.5, 8.1, 6.9, 9.2, 8.8, 7.6, 8.4, 9.0])\n\n# k and efficiency come from Part 2 and Part 3 and apply unchanged.\nrotor_power_2 = k * wind_speed_2**3\nelectrical_power_2 = rotor_power_2 * efficiency\n\nmean_power_2 = np.mean(electrical_power_2)\nspread_2 = np.std(electrical_power_2)\n\nprint(f\"Site 1: {mean_power:.1f} W (spread {spread:.1f} W)\")\nprint(f\"Site 2: {mean_power_2:.1f} W (spread {spread_2:.1f} W)\")\n\nprint(f\"Spread/mean site 1: {spread / mean_power:.2f}\")\nprint(f\"Spread/mean site 2: {spread_2 / mean_power_2:.2f}\")","position":{"start":{"line":211,"column":1},"end":{"line":226,"column":1}},"key":"PifGy7TXiY"},{"type":"paragraph","position":{"start":{"line":227,"column":1},"end":{"line":231,"column":1}},"children":[{"type":"text","value":"Site 2 delivers a considerably higher mean power, because the wind speeds are\nconsistently higher and the power grows with the third power. The absolute\nscatter is also larger at site 2. More meaningful is the ratio of scatter to\nmean: this value is smaller at site 2, so the power there is more even in\nrelative terms.","position":{"start":{"line":227,"column":1},"end":{"line":227,"column":1}},"key":"q6L1NEE9w9"}],"key":"sfbhkz8DDv"}],"class":"tip dropdown","key":"waJS4ocS39"}],"key":"QJJgAjDXsu"}],"key":"vwGrYJd9UK"},"references":{"cite":{"order":[],"data":{}}},"footer":{"navigation":{"prev":{"title":"2.1 NumPy Basics","url":"/chapter02-sec01","group":"2. NumPy & Matplotlib"},"next":{"title":"2.3 Diagrams with Matplotlib","url":"/chapter02-sec03","group":"2. NumPy & Matplotlib"}}},"domain":"http://localhost:3000"}